# album-studio .gitignore
# Last updated: 2026-08-09 (added .meta/ runtime state)
# Why: prevents re-spread of artifacts; see docs/STRUCTURE-POLICY.md.

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
# Local skill mirror (mirrored to OneDrive, not tracked here)
/.agents/

# --- Open Design artifacts (rebuildable, ~70 KB per prototype) ---
.od-skills/

# --- Placeholders (mark a not-yet-built subdirectory) ---
.placeholder
*.placeholder

# --- Local scratch / temp dumps ---
*.tmp
*.bak

# --- Large media outside the project (lives in OneDrive music-test-*) ---
# Music research sandboxes are large (200+ MB) and rebuildable.
# They're stored on disk for reference but not in git.
music/archive/

# Audio quality research: keep scripts + JSON data + reports; ignore mp3 outputs
# (rebuildable from music-3.0 with same brief)
planning/audio-quality-2026-07-30/*.mp3

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem

# --- Build artifacts (Phase 0.A test seed) ---
build/*.db
build/*.db-journal
build/*.db-wal

# --- Runtime state (machine-specific; rebuilt on first launch) ---
# .meta/ holds the SQLite database, daemon logs, schema drafts. None of
# this should be in version control — it varies per-host, per-run.
.meta/*.db
.meta/*.db-journal
.meta/*.db-wal
.meta/*.db-shm
.meta/daemon.log
.meta/daemon.lock
.meta/preview_daemon.log
.meta/preview_daemon.pid
# Allow the schema migrations + draft files to be tracked (they're code,
# not runtime state).
!.meta/migrations/
!.meta/album-studio-schema-draft.sql

# Test scratch dir (created 2026-08-09 for audit verification)
scratch/
